<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Leopold III Friedrich Franz</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1740–1817</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Leopold III, Duke of Anhalt-Dessau, Franz of Anhalt-Dessau</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Leopold III Friedrich Franz ruled Anhalt-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dessau">Dessau</a> from 1758, as prince and from 1807 as duke, until his death in 1817. A model <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/age-of-enlightenment">Enlightenment</a> ruler, he laid out the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dessau-worlitz-garden-realm">Dessau-Wörlitz Garden Realm</a>, the first large English-style landscape park in continental <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>, now a World Heritage Site. He promoted schools and agriculture and supported the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philanthropinum">Philanthropinum</a>, a progressive school founded in 1774.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/leopold-iii-frederick-franz.jpg" alt="Leopold III Friedrich Franz" width="320" height="409" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unidentified painter · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Leopold_III_of_Anhalt-Dessau.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
